## Analysis Performed

The project used:

- Descriptive analysis
- Time-series/trend analysis
- Correlation analysis
- Comparative analysis
- Data cleaning and preparation
- Data visualisation

The datasets were sourced from the **World Bank** and included GDP growth and inflation data. :contentReference[oaicite:2]{index=2}

## Key Finding

The analysis identified a **negative correlation of approximately -0.35** between South Africa's GDP growth and inflation in the analysed data. :contentReference[oaicite:3]{index=3}

The project also compared economic performance across the apartheid and post-apartheid periods to identify differences in GDP growth and inflation patterns.

